From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:29:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: integrate with the LuneOS Messaging app

The LuneOS IM transport (imlibpurpletransport) drives libpurple headless
for the webOS Messaging app. The app shows reactions, quotes, edits,
deletions and delivery ticks on the message bubble itself, which needs
structured data rather than the text renderings libpurple clients get.
This patch provides that data through process-wide purple signals and
conversation data that the transport registers and reads:

- reactions are emitted as "webos-im-reaction" instead of a "reacted
  with X" message; reactions from the app arrive through
  "webos-im-send-reaction" and go out through BuildReaction(), with the
  original sender taken from the message cache or, failing that, from
  the transport
- the server id of every message sent from the app is emitted as
  "webos-im-outbox-id", so the user can react to their own messages
- delivery and read receipts are emitted as "webos-im-receipt"
  ("webos-im-receipt-hwm" carries watermark receipts)
- edits and "delete for everyone" are emitted as "webos-im-edit" and
  "webos-im-delete" so the original bubble is updated in place
- the WhatsApp id of each received message, and the quoted message of
  a reply, are stashed as conversation data ("webos-msg-id",
  "webos-quoted-*"); replies from the app arrive as "webos-reply-to"
  and are sent as quotes
- poll votes from the app arrive through "webos-im-send-poll-vote" and
  are sent with BuildPollVote(); the message cache now records the raw
  sender, FromMe and IsGroup that BuildPollVote() needs
- locations, contact cards, events and polls are rendered as tokens and
  file:// links that the app turns into chips; link previews show their
  thumbnail, title and description; stickers are transcoded from WebP
  to PNG because the webOS WebKit has no WebP decoder; WebP files sent
  from the app go out as stickers; received documents keep their real
  file name; a video's thumbnail is saved next to it as its poster; an
  image and its caption are delivered as one message
- WhatsApp Channels (newsletters) are shown: their names are fetched on
  connect, joining one fetches its recent history, and posts seen twice
  (offline sync and history) are dropped; the "ignore-newsletters"
  option therefore defaults to off. Status updates are routed to a
  per-sender "<phone>@broadcast" chat instead of a 1:1 chat
- deleting a WhatsApp account removes only that account's device from
  the shared whatsmeow store ("account-removed")
- defaults suited to the device: a 500-message cache (replies and
  reactions need it), profile pictures on ("preview"), group subjects
  fetched on connect, and a lost buddy icon is re-fetched

The quote strings added to gowhatsapp_message are freed in
gowhatsapp_free_message().

Rebased onto 1.27.0, where incoming text is HTML-escaped in Go and
outgoing HTML is stripped in Go: the escape argument of
gowhatsapp_display_text_message() is gone, and the caption folded into
the media message is escaped where it is built.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
